# Vue

Use `<script setup lang="ts">`. One component per file. Type props and emits.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
defineProps<{
  saveLocally: boolean
}>()

const emit = defineEmits<{
  'update:saveLocally': [value: boolean]
  clear: []
}>()
</script>
```

- Views in `src/views` compose widgets from `src/components`.
- Read and write session state through `useSession`. Views do not touch `localStorage`.
- Buttons that do not submit a form use `type="button"`.
- Keep controls labeled. Preserve the skip link, focus moves after navigation, and `aria-invalid` on failed items.
- Reach for an existing daisyUI component class before writing a custom control. Styling rules are in `tailwind-daisyui.mdc`.
